    title: "Lunch - actually taking a break"
    at: "-1d 12:30 / -1d 13:15"
    notes:
      - created: "-1d 13:20"
        content: |
          Walked through the park near the office. Bought a sandwich from the cart.

          Sat on a bench. Didn't check my phone (much).

          Hal would be proud. He's always telling me to "exist in real time occasionally."

          I'm trying.

  # Day +1: Congressional briefing and alliance building
  - type: event
    priority_ref: active
    title: "Congressional briefing - moderate caucus"
    at: "+1d 10:00 / +1d 11:30"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
      pinned: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 11:45"
        content: |
          Briefed 12 congressional moderates on the climate proposal.

          **Their questions (translation in parentheses):**

          1. "What's the budget impact?" (How much will this cost me politically?)
          → Showed the $8B direct vs $50B total leverage. Emphasized private sector role.

          2. "What if the private sector doesn't participate?" (What's the risk?)
          → Historical PPP data shows strong participation when properly structured.

          3. "Why climate and not domestic infrastructure?" (Why this priority?)
          → This IS infrastructure. It's just infrastructure that happens to be strategic positioning abroad.

          4. "What's the timeline for returns?" (When do we get credit?)
          → Phase 1 results in 18 months. Early wins for midterm messaging.

          **Reactions:**
          - 8 favorable (will support)
          - 3 neutral (need more data, probably yes)
          - 1 skeptical (might oppose, but won't lead opposition)

          That's enough. That's a winning coalition.

          Austin will follow up individually. We're building the votes.
        mentions:
          - ganon

  - type: action
    priority_ref: strategic
    title: "Brief Stuart on congressional response"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+1d"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 12:30"
        content: |
          Need to update Stuart on US congressional support so he can use it to strengthen UK position internally.

          "US has congressional buy-in" is a powerful argument for UK Treasury to participate.

          Will schedule call for tomorrow.
        mentions:
          - stuart

  - type: note
    priority_ref: active
