          title: White House Feedback
          href: mailto:mara.tierney@state.gov
        mentions:
          - chief_staff

  - type: event
    priority_ref: household
    title: "Evening call with Hal - actual good news"
    at: "+1d 19:30 / +1d 20:00"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 20:10"
        content: |
          **Signal video call**

          Told Hal about the White House approval.

          **Hal:** "You did it. Turned an impossible ask into a bipartisan infrastructure win."

          **Me:** "I just... changed the words."

          **Hal:** "You changed the story. That's everything."

          He's proud. I can tell. It's nice to hear.

          **Hal:** "I'm in DC next week. Wednesday through Friday."

          **Me:** "I'm here all week."

          **Hal:** "Dinner Wednesday? Actual dinner, not working dinner?"

          **Me:** "Deal."

          Finally. Same city. Same time zone. Same dinner table.
        mentions:
          - hal
    tags:
      star: [user]

  # Day +2: Alliance management
  - type: event
    priority_ref: strategic
    title: "Stuart Hayford - update call"
    at: "+2d 09:00 / +2d 09:30"
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 09:40"
        content: |
          **Video call with Stuart**

          Briefed him on congressional support and White House preliminary approval.

          **Stuart:** "That's faster than I expected."

          **Me:** "Made it easy to say yes."

          **Stuart:** "UK Treasury is still nervous, but if I can show them US commitment with congressional backing, that changes the equation."

          **Me:** "Use the economic angle. US participation means US companies, which means procurement opportunities for UK firms in the supply chain."

          **Stuart:** "Clever. I'll work that angle."

          He'll brief UK Treasury next week. Feeling confident.
        mentions:
          - stuart

  - type: event
    priority_ref: strategic
    title: "EU partner coordination - video conference"
    at: "+2d 14:00 / +2d 15:15"
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 15:30"
        content: |
          **Video conference with EU partners (Veronica, Alouette, others)**

          Presented the final proposal. Emphasized EU co-leadership, shared governance, strategic partnership.

          **Veronica (EU):** "This is exactly what we discussed. Well-structured."

          **Alouette (France):** [slight pause] "We've been developing a similar framework. Perhaps we should coordinate?"

          **Me:** "Absolutely. This works better with aligned partnership. Would love to incorporate French perspectives."

          *(Translation: You're late, but we'll let you claim you shaped it.)*

          **Alouette:** "I'll share our draft. I'm sure we can find alignment."

          **Me:** "I'm confident we will."

          France will join. They'll make some cosmetic changes and claim co-authorship. That's fine.

          The fund will exist. That's what matters.
        mentions:
          - ronnie
          - alouette
    tags:
      star: [user]

  - type: note
    priority_ref: active
    title: "Updated timeline - proposal advancement"
    created: "-1d"
    tags:
      pinned: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "-1d 20:00"
        content: |
          **Climate Finance Proposal - Advancement Timeline**

          **Week of Apr 21:**
          - White House formal approval (expected)
          - UK Treasury briefing (Stuart handling)
          - French integration discussions (Alouette coordinating)

          **Week of Apr 28:**
          - Full partner meeting (US, EU, UK, France)
          - Draft framework agreement
          - Begin Phase 1 planning

          **Week of May 5:**
          - Congressional committee presentations
          - Partner formal commitments
          - Public announcement (joint US-EU-UK statement)

          **Summer 2025:**
          - Phase 1 launch (pilot program)
          - First project selections
          - Private sector solicitation

          It's happening. A year of groundwork. Months of language refinement. Weeks of alliance building.

          Now it's just... happening.

  - type: action
    priority_ref: policy
    title: "Draft joint announcement statement"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+2d"
    tags:
      todo: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 17:00"
        content: |
          **@plot, draft a joint announcement statement for US-EU-UK climate partnership that emphasizes shared leadership and strategic infrastructure**
        ai_query: true
      - created: "+2d 17:00"
        content: |
          **Plot AI Response:**

          **Draft Joint Announcement**

          **United States, European Union, and United Kingdom Launch Global Climate Resilience Partnership**

          Today, the United States, European Union, and United Kingdom announce the formation of the Global Climate Resilience Partnership (GCRP), a groundbreaking public-private infrastructure initiative that will mobilize $50 billion to build climate-resilient infrastructure in developing nations while creating economic opportunities and strengthening strategic partnerships.

          This partnership represents a new model of international cooperation: fiscally responsible, private sector-enabled, and focused on delivering measurable results. By leveraging public investment to unlock private capital, GCRP will amplify impact while ensuring sustainable program governance.

          "This partnership demonstrates that climate action and economic leadership are not competing priorities - they are complementary strategies," said US Secretary of State William Dennison.

          GCRP will launch a pilot program in 2025, supporting climate resilience projects in three regions with proven economic and environmental benefits.

          [Additional quotes from EU and UK leadership]
      - created: "+2d 17:15"
        content: |
          ---

          Good start. Will refine with State Department communications and coordinate with EU/UK messaging teams.

          Everyone needs to feel like they're leading. That's the key to multilateral success.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: household
    title: "Hal arrives Wednesday - dinner plans"
    created: "+2d"
    tags:
