  - type: event
    priority_ref: household
    title: "Dinner with Hal - finally same city"
    at: "+3d 19:00 / +3d 21:30"
    tags:
      pinned: [user]
      star: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+3d 22:00"
        content: |
          Quiet restaurant. Good food. No phones on the table.

          Talked about everything except work (for the first hour, anyway). Then talked about work because we can't help it.

          **Hal:** "Do you think it'll actually happen? The climate fund?"

          **Me:** "Yes. Because I made it impossible to say no without looking unreasonable."

          **Hal:** "That's your superpower. Making the hard thing look like the obvious thing."

          **Me:** "I just... change the language."

          **Hal:** "It's not just language. It's narrative. It's making people believe they want what you need them to want."

          Maybe. I don't know. I just do the work.

          **Hal:** "I'm proud of you."

          **Me:** "I'm glad you're here."

          We stayed until the restaurant closed. Walked back to the hotel. Held hands.

          For a few hours, the world was very small and very simple.

          It was nice.
        mentions:
          - hal

  - type: note
    priority_ref: policy
    title: "Reflection - how this works"
    created: "+3d"
    notes:
      - created: "+3d 23:00"
        content: |
          A year ago, someone said "we need a climate fund" and I thought "that's impossible."

          Not impossible. Just impossible with those words.

          So I changed the words:
          - Fund → Partnership
          - Commitment → Investment
          - Aid → Infrastructure
          - Binding → Phased

          Same outcomes. Different story.

          That's the work. That's what diplomacy is.

          Not lying. Not manipulation.

          Just finding the language that lets people choose to do the thing they're afraid to choose.

          Making progress look inevitable instead of controversial.

          Making the right choice look obvious instead of risky.

          Hal says it's my superpower. Maybe. Or maybe it's just stubbornness combined with vocabulary.

          Either way, the fund will exist. Projects will get built. Climate resilience will improve.

          And everyone will think it was their idea.

          That's how it works. That's how it has to work.

          No headlines about me. Just headlines about the partnership.

          That's the job.
